  <ferc:ReportYear id="HH660FC444EE17A785BFF22BCDC6434313" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4" decimals="0" unitRef="HHferc_us_Pure">2025</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="HHBD1AFC97EAE2BF213BAE5A53CD7CEAC7" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">Q4</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:IndicatorStockholdersReportSubmittedOrNotPrepared id="HH338A37446FF58C0756F3AE1CD8A44F64" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">Not Prepared</ferc:IndicatorStockholdersReportSubmittedOrNotPrepared>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Note 1&amp;#8212;Overview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;On June 1, 2023, Par Rocky Mountain Midstream, LLC (&amp;#8220;PRMM&amp;#8221;) acquired the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC'')-regulated Silvertip Pipeline system from ExxonMobil Corporation (&amp;#8220;Exxon&amp;#8221;). This acquisition occurred concurrently with Par Pacific Holdings, Inc.&amp;#8217;s ("Par") acquisition of a 63,000 barrels per day ("bpd") refinery (&amp;#8220;Billings Refinery&amp;#8221;) and associated marketing and logistics assets in Billings, MT from Exxon and two of its subsidiaries. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;The Silvertip Pipeline system is a crude pipeline with receipt points at Silvertip Station, Edgar Station, and Laurel Terminal, Montana, and delivery points into CHS Inc&amp;#8217;s ("CHS") refinery in Laurel, Montana, and the Billings Refinery in Billings, Montana. Installed in 1949, the Silvertip Pipeline is a 12-inch pipeline with a capacity of 55,000 bpd. It spans a length of 70 miles originating at Silvertip Station and terminating at the Billings Refinery. Silvertip Pipeline is the primary supplier of crude for the Billings Refinery; it provides 60-75% of total crude deliveries into the refinery.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;PRMM is a wholly owned subsidiary of Par Petroleum, LLC (&amp;#8220;PPLLC&amp;#8221;, the &amp;#8220;Parent&amp;#8221;); PPLLC is a wholly owned subsidiary of Par. Affiliates of PRMM include Par Montana, LLC ("PML"), Par Hawaii Shared Services ("PHSS"), and other wholly owned subsidiaries of the Parent and Par (collectively, the "Affiliates").&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Note 2&amp;#8212;Summary of Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;PRMM&amp;#8217;s financial statements and the accompanying notes are prepared in conformity with the FERC&amp;#8217;s Uniform System of Accounts (18 C.F.R. Part 352) &amp;#8220;USofA&amp;#8221;. As a result of PRMM&amp;#8217;s election to apply pushdown accounting upon the June 1, 2023 acquisitions, PRMM's financial statements reflect a basis of accounting based on the allocation of Par&amp;#8217;s purchase price.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Use of Estimates &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;The preparation of financial statements in accordance with the USofA requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets, liabilities, revenues and expenses, and the related disclosures. Actual amounts could differ from these estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Cash and cash equivalents consist of all highly liquid investments with original maturities of three months or less. The carrying value of cash equivalents approximates fair value because of the short-term nature of these investments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Allowance for Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;PRMM is exposed to credit losses primarily through non-payment of its crude transportation invoices. Credit limits and/or prepayment requirements are set based on such factors as the customer&amp;#8217;s financial results, credit rating, payment history, and industry and are reviewed annually for customers with material credit limits. Credit allowances are reviewed at least annually based on changes in the customer&amp;#8217;s creditworthiness due to economic conditions, liquidity, and business strategy as publicly reported and through discussions between the customer and the PRMM. PRMM establishes provisions for losses on trade receivables based on the estimated credit loss it expects to incur over the life of the receivable. PRMM did not have any allowances on trade receivables during the years ended December 31, 2025 or 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Inventories&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;PRMM values materials and supplies, which include spare parts, at average cost. PRMM does not own any commodity inventory; all the line-fill inventory on the Silvertip Pipeline system belongs to PML or CHS, the shippers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Property, Plant, and Equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; text-indent: .45in; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;PRMM capitalizes the cost of additions and major improvements and modifications to property, plant, and equipment. The cost of repairs and normal maintenance of property, plant, and equipment is expensed as incurred. Major improvements and modifications of property, plant, and equipment are those expenditures that either extend the useful life, increase the capacity, or improve the operating efficiency of the asset or the safety of PRMM&amp;#8217;s operations. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; text-indent: .45in; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;PRMM filed a Request for Approval of Initial Property Account Depreciation Rates (DO24-5-000) on May 22, 2024, which was approved on August 16, 2024. The initial FERC depreciation rates were effective January 1, 2024, and utilized for the 2024 and 2025 year-to-date depreciation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; text-indent: .45in; line-height: normal; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none; margin: 8.1pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none;"&gt;Rates commencing January 1, 2024, and utilized on a go-forward basis:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div align="center"&gt;
