&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Note 6&amp;#8212;Debt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;Guarantee&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;On February 28, 2023, the Parent and Par Petroleum Finance Corp., an affiliate of the Parent, (collectively, the "Borrowers") entered into a $550.0 million term loan facility with Wells Fargo Bank, National Association, as administrative agent, and the lenders party thereto from time to time (the "Term Loan Credit Agreement"). During 2024, the Term Loan Credit Agreement was amended to increase the size of the term loan to $650.0 million. The Term Loan Credit Agreement bears interest at a fluctuating rate per annum, requires quarterly payments of $1.6 million, and matures on February 28, 2030. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Term Loan Credit Agreement had an outstanding loan balance of $633.6 million and $640.1 million, respectively. Following PRMM&amp;#8217;s commencement of activities on June 1, 2023, the Term Loan Credit Agreement was secured by first priority liens (subject to the relative priority of permitted liens) on substantially all of the property and assets of PRMM, in addition to the property of certain other Affiliates of the Parent, other than assets that secure the ABL Credit Facility (defined below) and assets that secure intermediation facilities of any such entities, subject to certain customary exceptions.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;The Term Loan Credit Agreement is fully and unconditionally guaranteed on a senior secured basis,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;jointly and severally, by PRMM and certain other Affiliates of the Parent, and is guaranteed on a senior unsecured basis only as to the payment of principal and interest by Par.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif;"&gt;On April&amp;#160;26, 2023, Par, the Parent, PRMM, and certain other Affiliates entered into an Asset-Based Revolving Credit Agreement with certain lenders, and Wells Fargo Bank, National Association, as administrative agent and collateral agent (as amended from time to time, the &amp;#8220;ABL Credit Facility&amp;#8221;), providing for a senior secured asset-based revolving credit facility in an initial aggregate principal amount of up to $150&amp;#160;million and secured by a first priority lien over PRMM&amp;#8217;s and certain other Affiliates&amp;#8217; assets and other personal property, subject to certain customary exceptions. During 2023 and 2024, other amendments were made to the ABL Credit Facility that increased the revolving facility to $1.4 billion. The interest rates applicable to borrowings under the ABL Credit Facility are based on a fluctuating rate of interest measured by reference to either, at Par&amp;#8217;s option, (i) a base rate, plus an applicable margin, or (ii) an Adjusted Term SOFR rate, plus an applicable margin. The ABL Credit Facility will mature, and the commitments thereunder will terminate on April&amp;#160;26, 2028.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Note 7&amp;#8212;Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;In the ordinary course of business, PRMM is a party to various lawsuits and other contingent matters. PRMM establishes accruals for specific legal matters when it determines that the likelihood of an unfavorable outcome is probable and the loss is reasonably estimable. It is possible that an unfavorable outcome of one or more of these lawsuits or other contingencies could have a material impact on PRMM&amp;#8217;s balance sheet, income statement, or cash flows&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Periodically, PRMM receives communications from various federal, state, and local governmental authorities asserting violations of environmental laws and/or regulations. These governmental entities may also propose or assess fines or require corrective actions for these asserted violations. PRMM does not anticipate that any such matters currently asserted will have a material impact on its balance sheet, income statement, or cash flows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Note 8&amp;#8212;Benefit Plans&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Par maintains a defined contribution plan for employees, including those of PRMM. All eligible employees may participate in the Par plan after thirty days of service. For all employees participating in the Par plan, PRMM matches employee contributions up to a maximum of 6% of the employee&amp;#8217;s eligible compensation, with the employer contributions vesting at 100%. For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, PRMM made contributions to the plans totaling approximately $31 thousand and $139 thousand, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Note 9&amp;#8212;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin;"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Company recorded $2.4 million and $2.1 million in income tax expenses primarily driven by operating income from the respective periods. At December 31, 2025 and 2024, the net receivable with the Parent in the Receivables from Affiliated Companies line item includes a $4.7 million and $2.6 million payable, respectively, related to income taxes as, under the intercompany tax sharing agreement, PRMM is required to remit its allocated portion of estimated taxes payable to the Parent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin;"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, income tax expense was different from the amounts computed by applying U.S. Federal income tax rate of 21% to pretax income as a result of the following:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div align="center"&gt;
