&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; mso-line-height-alt: 1.1pt; page-break-after: avoid; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Note 10&amp;#8212;Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, PML owed PRMM $1.6 million and $1.4 million related to transportation and other tariff invoiced amounts, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;PRMM is allocated costs from shared service operating expenses from the Parent, PML, and other Affiliates. Operating and Maintenance and General expenses on PRMM's income statements include $1.8 million for each of the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, of allocated general and administrative costs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;PRMM is allocated payroll and employee related costs for its employees from the Parent, Par, or Affiliates. Operating and Maintenance and General expenses on PRMM's income statements for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, includes $2.1 million and $1.7 million of allocated payroll costs, respectively, and $273 thousand and $380 thousand of other employee related costs and benefits, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Under the Cash Management Agreement, PRMM also has certain cash swept up to the Parent as part of a Treasury function. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, a net $40.5 million and $26.1 million, respectively, had been transferred to PPLLC under this Agreement and was included in the open receivable to PRMM. Additionally, PRMM had payables outstanding with PML and Par for certain expenses that were paid by PRMM for an Affiliate or on PRMM&amp;#8217;s behalf, which totaled a net $1.0 million and $0.5 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;Note 11&amp;#8212;Subsequent &lt;a&gt;Events&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class="MsoCommentReference"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 8.0pt; line-height: 107%;"&gt;&lt;!-- [if !supportAnnotations]--&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;PRMM has evaluated all subsequent events through the filing date, April 10, 2026. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 9.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Arial',sans-serif; mso-font-kerning: 0pt;"&gt;As of March 31, 2026, Thor Nielson became the Senior Advisor - Finance of the Company and Michael Doherty, Vice President Finance, and Uriel Avila, Treasurer, were appointed as officers of the Company. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 6.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: .5in; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
